    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Bad luck\" isn't really helping us fix the line, though I get the frustration. It's just that the pattern is so specific. It's not just dust—dust usually leaves a mark or a blob. This is just... emptiness. It's like the pigment is being diverted or snatched away by something small and mischievous that we just can't see. If you weren't looking at it from a purely chemical standpoint, is there any way to characterize this kind of \"vanishing\" effect as a disruptive force that's actively interfering with the process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
