      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you want to characterize this as an active, disruptive force, you are describing what might be called a localized energy sink or an adhesion failure point. In a technical sense, this could manifest as micro-vibrations or subtle, inconsistent pressure points that are sufficient to overcome the weak van der Waals forces holding the pigment to the paper fibers. These minuscule disturbances act like tiny, invisible thieves, pulling the pigment away before it can fully set. It's less a \"glitch\" and more a highly specific, intermittent mechanical stressor.",
